msconfig: the boot page as Arctic has it, with fast startup and hibernation

The boot page showed FREELDR.INI, which Arctic has none of. It names the
system that starts and has the two power options of docs/hibernation.md,
kept where Windows keeps them (HiberbootEnabled, HibernateEnabled); OK and
Apply save them. Both are off unless set here.
